D. Cognitive Analysis Module
1) Clinical Rationale and Task Design: NeuroLens digitizes two clinically validated instruments targeting processing speed, attention, and working memory — established prodromal markers of PD driven by early basal ganglia and dopaminergic degeneration. In TMT-A, users sequentially connect 25 numbered touchscreen dots; total completion time (seconds) is recorded. In SDMT, users perform symbol-to-digit matching within 60 seconds; scores are scaled ×1.5 (sdmtotal = correct_matches × 1.5) to align with PPMI's 90-second standard administration.
2) Dataset and Target Encoding: The module is trained on the PPMI Curated Data Cut comprising 4,267 unique baseline patients: 336 Healthy Controls (target: 0) and 3,931 PD Spectrum patients (COHORT = 1 confirmed PD and COHORT = 4 prodromal; target: 1). SWEDD participants are excluded to avoid label ambiguity. Analysis is restricted to a
