4) Model Training and Validation Pipeline: Data is partitioned into an 80% train-validation pool and 20% stratified held-out test set. A 5-fold StratifiedGroupKFold (grouped by PATNO) ensures complete patient isolation. Logistic Regression, Random Forest, XGBoost, Gradient Boosting, and a Stacking ensemble were benchmarked via AUC-ROC with Youden's J thresholding. XGBoost was selected based on superior holdout generalization (AUC
0.8011) over GBM (0.7897), despite GBM marginally leading in cross-validation (0.8310 vs. 0.8268).
5) Calibration, Threshold Selection, and Output: The XGBoost model is post-hoc probability-calibrated via Platt scaling (CalibratedClassifierCV, sigmoid, cv=5) to ensure well-calibrated posterior probabilities suitable for late fusion. The optimal classification threshold (0.4364) is derived via Youden's J statistic from aggregated out-of-fold crossvalidation predictions rather than the held-out set to prevent threshold overfitting:
J = maxθ (Sensitivityθ + Specificityθ − 1) (3)
Risk is further contextualized through a five-block visual percentile indicator (p10, p25, p50, p75, p90) derived from holdout-set probability distributions. Per-patient SHAP values computed on the uncalibrated model expose top contributing features at inference time. The module emits a standardized JSON payload {risk_probability, percentile_rank, contributing_factors} consumed by the late fusion layer described in Section IV.
V. MULTIMODAL RISK FUSION
A. AUC-Weighted Late Fusion:
To combine predictions across modalities with different discriminative power, NeuroLens uses an AUC-weighted late fusion strategy. Each modality's normalized risk score -# . /0,12is weighted by its holdout AUC value %#:
R_final = ( Σ_{i . M} w_i · s_i ) / ( Σ_{i . M} w_i )
where 3 is the set of available modalities for the session.
AUC-weighted fusion was preferred over equal weighting (which ignores validated performance differences across modules), single-modality (which discards complementary information), and learned fusion (which requires a unified multi-modality training cohort unavailable at this stage). The scheme is transparent, deterministic, updatable per module, and degrades gracefully when modalities are missing by renormalizing over available channels.
